Z||000000||superXmotorsports||11-05-1999||09:34 PM||||Can anyone tell me how much for a new set of heads and where the best place is to buy.  I checked alot of the old threads and came up empty.  Thanks!||||reg||4
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||11-05-1999||09:46 PM||||You did not specify for what engine. If its a V6 make sure you don't get the 2.8 heads from the camaro/firebird. They had SMALLER valves!!! The Fiero uses the same heads used on the 3.4 in the 91-95 f-bodies.<BR>If its a 4 cyl, I wouldn't know where the best prices are we have been extrmely lucky with no cracks...so far.||||reg||1
Z||000002||superXmotorsports||11-05-1999||10:18 PM||||I bought a 3.2L stroked stock Fiero motor that dosen't have heads.  Rather than strip them off the 2.8 in my GT now I would like to buy a pair and have them p/p for the new motor.  I'm looking for a price and the best place to buy them.  Thanks!||||reg||4
Z||000003||BENGAL4||11-05-1999||10:59 PM||||A boneyard near my house has a pair of 2.8L Fiero heads laying in a van. Don't know what condition they are in. I bought the exhaust manifolds from the same engine and they are in great shape. I can see what he wants for them if you are interested. I am in SW Ohio.||||reg||6
Z||000004||mwbackus||11-05-1999||11:55 PM||||"New" heads from GM Performance (part # 14054884) are available for $366.75 each.<P>Source :<P>Lustine Chevrolet<BR>4510 Longfellow St. Hyattsville Md 20781<BR>1-800-638-0514 <A HREF="http://www.lustineparts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lustineparts.com/</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||superXmotorsports||11-06-1999||02:02 AM||||Thanks for the help!  For $600 I think I'll have the existing heads checked and probably used.||||reg||14
Z||000006||batboy||11-06-1999||06:53 AM||||SuperX, the Fiero 2.8 heads are what the factory calls HO heads (HO=high output). They have bigger valves than the regular 2.8 cast iron heads. There are some HO heads used on a few 3.4 Camaros that had a slightly bigger exhaust valve than even the Fiero heads. Of course, bigger valves mean increased flow and more horsepower.||||reg||1
Z||000007||superXmotorsports||11-06-1999||09:58 AM||||Do they run about the same $ batboy?  I don't mind spending the money if it is a reasonable gain.  I will probably have about $800 of work done to the heads in addition to the cost.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000008||Bruce||11-06-1999||12:01 PM||||Why not check with Ed Parks- he seems to have everything. Alot of the guys here know his www and phone #.||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||11-07-1999||04:53 AM||||I don't know the current prices of heads. What I would do is call around to several salvage yards and ask for a price quote on a set of 3.4 heads. This will determine what the normal cost will be. Then go over with a measuring caliper and find a HO set with the large valves. If they quoted you a price already over the phone, they'll have to sell you the HO set of heads for that price.<P>As SuperX indicated, you must be willing to spend some cash rebuilding a set of heads if you want the engine to make the maximum amount of power. It's all about flow. Fuel mixture flowing in and exhaust flowing out. The better the flow, the more power.||||reg||1
Z||000010||mwbackus||11-07-1999||11:11 AM||||I pay about $200 for a complete port and bowl blend for a set of heads.  If you need something to start with, just get some junk cores and send them here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.bluechipmotor.com/cylinderheads.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bluechipmotor.com/cylinderheads.html</A> <P>For $80 (and the cores) you get a set of rebuilt heads:  cleaned, magnefluxed, and re-surfaced, with a 3-angle valve job.  <BR>(Note:  It cost me $100 more to get the same work done locally, but I wanted new valves so I had no choice.)<BR>Add a $200 port & polish and your total machining cost would be around $300.<P>In case anyone is interested, here are the Comp Cams part numbers / prices(summit) for the components I used:<P>1414-12  	1.6:1 ROCKERS 		$133.99<P>980-12   	VALVE SPRINGS		$ 38.69<P>7816-12  	PUSHRODS 		$ 29.69<P>742-12		RETAINERS		$ 45.39<P>601-12      	VALVE LOCKS & CAPS	$  7.39<P>501-12      	VALVE SEALS		$  6.69 <P>A total of $261.84 plus $6.95 shipping.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||RICK||11-08-1999||11:00 AM||||SupperX-- I e-mailed my buddy that owns a salvage yard to see if he had any or if he can get a set cheap, I'll post back if he finds any.<p>[This message has been edited by RICK (edited 11-08-1999).]||||reg||1
